# Composable Hub Standards

## Every Candidate Feature Is a Block

The candidate hub is a blank slate. Every feature (DOT app, MVR, resume, portfolio, etc.)
is a self-contained block with its own component, its own Zustand store, and its own data.
The hub itself is stateless — it only reads `useHubBlocksStore` and renders.

## Adding a New Block

1. Add a `BlockDefinition` entry to `src/lib/block-registry.ts`
2. Create the block component in `src/components/blocks/[BlockName]Block.tsx`
3. Create the block's store in `src/stores/[block-name]-block-store.ts`
4. Lazy-import the component in `CandidateShell`
5. No schema changes needed — `hub_blocks.block_type` is open text
6. Add data tables in `block-data.ts` if the block stores data (see `block-development.mdc`)

## Every Block MUST Use `BlockCard` as Its Outer Wrapper

```tsx
// BAD — custom card shell
<div className="bg-white rounded-2xl border ...">
  <h3>DOT Application</h3>
  ...
</div>

// GOOD
import BlockCard from '@/components/ui/BlockCard'
import { ClipboardList } from 'lucide-react'

<BlockCard
  icon={ClipboardList}
  title="DOT Application"
  description="Federal driver qualification file"
  status="in-progress"
  onRemove={handleRemove}
>
  {/* block content */}
</BlockCard>
```

## Block Status

Derive `status` from the block's own store — never from the hub:

```tsx
// GOOD — block owns its completion status
const { isComplete, hasStarted } = useDotBlockStore()
const status = isComplete ? 'complete' : hasStarted ? 'in-progress' : 'empty'
```

## The Career Card Is Read-Only

The career card is a projection of whatever blocks the user has installed.
It contains **zero logic** — only rendering. It receives block data and displays it.
Never add data fetching or business logic to the career card.

## Block Registry Is the Source of Truth

All block metadata (label, description, icon, category, suggestedFor keywords)
lives in `src/lib/block-registry.ts`. Never hardcode block labels or categories
in UI components — always read from the registry.

```tsx
// BAD
<h3>DOT Application</h3>

// GOOD
import { getBlockDefinition } from '@/lib/block-registry'
const def = getBlockDefinition(block.blockType)
<BlockCard icon={...} title={def.label} description={def.description} ...>
```

## Do NOT Add Features to Legacy Shells

`DriverShell` and `DeveloperShell` are frozen. All new candidate features are blocks
wired through `CandidateShell`. If you are tempted to add a new `if (currentPage === '...')`
case to `DriverShell` or `DeveloperShell`, STOP — create a block instead.
